{"title":"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(wowe)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (wowe)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider all quadrilaterals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23446454eb9fccfe9b792aee481326e9a93c8b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8bf6a33fda7064bc18de335471565522d1147a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=9$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/755800db4e2f4bcf1958e9009f36ce8b09a93cc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=7$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2dddbf064a45fe6ccdce27d76eca2f87b5369dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. What is the radius of the largest possible circle that fits inside or on the boundary of such a quadrilateral?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee3b1e676debcbc7034d97cde188651f9a77c096.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\sqrt{15} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\sqrt{21} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\sqrt{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 2\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"446\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note as above that ABCD must be tangential to obtain the circle with maximal radius. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the points on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> respectively where the circle is tangent. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/870bd4e7e7d40b2bfa324853d7ec4ef1014c2336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=\\angle BAD$\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/728963c4921c823fe45e2e97f463b3fba636a9d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha=\\angle ADC$\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" />. Since the quadrilateral is cyclic(because we want to maximize the circle, so we set the quadrilateral to be cyclic), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a1184d41f201179eb55444d3a845b0cfe11cba91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC=180^{\\circ}-\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/5403d3e5c22b3becc3fb50d091c4f9f0e2488428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCD=180^{\\circ}-\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"147\" height=\"13\" />. Let the circle have center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5c5aae3a2e4f7c28e415432df0119b556f040f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OHD$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d3dd849052f9a889796920dd3d7dcb6e816d3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OGC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/c/44cc455fb75ab658fa40b887505970e7a4122684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OFB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b993f0fe6fd7f85c4fd135b6fee75f4200431ab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OEA$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> are right angles. \n</p><p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f0847e000d7be2e83c751c21ac50d1cec854dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FOG=\\theta$\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f56b843355e2cb58b9b6f2b41dcda465ac949446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GOH=180^{\\circ}-\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97da0bb17b15090fce31d2870391269f0edd8bc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EOH=180^{\\circ}-\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc054e962cfd97d212ea84df0c340bc97491326c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FOE=\\alpha$\" width=\"78\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/7758341c74d404fb0083c0de0628d0f7255a69d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEOH\\sim OFCG$\" width=\"140\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4fcfea12c0b33ad3430e393bce8d214d57460b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EBFO\\sim HOGD$\" width=\"142\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/7/f075d8e77b16e2e748b49a47fdce475219b6ecdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=CG$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3e56f92344bf5332032c7d9818ed749bc50c68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF=x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16c894a061c85dbdf6f6acf035f57e3718079c91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF=BE=9-x$\" width=\"148\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3ae79ff3fa6d4dc3862617c6bb4b975046c46b42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GD=DH=7-x$\" width=\"152\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/2936d5abdee5e37087979dbc83fff67a09f17aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH=AE=x+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"148\" height=\"14\" />. Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/7758341c74d404fb0083c0de0628d0f7255a69d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEOH\\sim OFCG$\" width=\"140\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4fcfea12c0b33ad3430e393bce8d214d57460b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EBFO\\sim HOGD$\" width=\"142\" height=\"12\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1c3ef8a215e1a5409942f88dadfb187971b734e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r/(x+5)=x/r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/9/8695e0a6ff7f6d2df2d9d2a8a13d7b25238740fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9-x)/r=r/(7-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />. By equating the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2221c84f16a3f75ae07e5023384cc40d9c05357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> from each, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f90504bb587c2746c8a272f7651a258d7c05b679.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x+5)=(7-x)(9-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" />. Solving we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b022dc8ef6d33931fc1ae3d27df3ea0a81b52936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfe79efccfc86efb2d1976a24423fe54cf3148f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\sqrt{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"112\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To maximize the radius of the circle, we also need to maximize its area. To maximize the area of the circle, the quadrilateral must be tangential (have an incircle). In a tangential quadrilateral, the sum of opposite sides is equal to the semiperimeter of the quadrilateral. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d93f76ed341e0487f837eacc7f68bfe6cf468b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14+7=12+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />, so this particular quadrilateral has an incircle. By definition, given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> side lengths, a cyclic quadrilateral has the maximum area of any quadrilateral with those side lengths. Therefore, to maximize the area of the quadrilateral and thus the incircle, we assume that this quadrilateral is cyclic. \n</p><p>For cyclic quadrilaterals, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Brahmagupta%27s_formula\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Brahmagupta&#39;s formula\">Brahmagupta's formula</a> gives the area as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec165011b7b836e991da4bf263b05d932f056b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)(s-d)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"232\" height=\"32\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the semiperimeter and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d02bb2275100261109b043261e702124460a83e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are the side lengths. Breaking it up into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles, we see the area of a tangential quadrilateral is also equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d84c3c39b42fb2b850558fa117ecb2df8c1233d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r*s$\" width=\"34\" height=\"8\" />. Equate these two equations.\nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, the semiperimeter, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, the area and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />,we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/831c7cde6aa3012d53ba135c93cdb7643a8f40f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\sqrt{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"79\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Trigonometry)\">Solution 3 (Trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Pitot's Theorem, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b7a610ca1c6be229c1c4446ebfc737cd3fd1e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB+CD=AD+BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"185\" height=\"14\" />, there exists a circle tangent to all four sides of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, we need to find the radius of this circle.\n</p><p>Let the circle be tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/2/c221aa0f4e42ee53e3978bcabe86bb40784c953e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=x$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/8/0f861cdd52e65580668061b0eaf3c023960029f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AS$\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" /> also equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Let the center of the circle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> bisects angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54816fea57fb256afb3ef76c68eb60f0b5361f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot\\frac{A}{2}=\\frac{x}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />. Moreover, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24fce7f1e4509aa7e9f1e04086fd8f444bf5366d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot\\frac{C}{2}=\\frac{9-(14-x)}{r}=\\frac{x-5}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"238\" height=\"38\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a331d22c95ae8c03f354e9f96dfe81a0a4aa9d09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle \\frac{C}{2}=90^\\circ-\\angle \\frac{A}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"136\" height=\"39\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295dcb5d2891efa3f0b96014b1c289ada45821b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot\\frac{C}{2}=\\tan\\frac{A}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" />, and we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34b277ba5193535cdbfc07bbf7497a8cdf69ddd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{r}{x}=\\frac{x-5}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e5bc3e3ebd46ba5c609f373a374b14937e96d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2=x(x-5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6c05ac606355f55b80c54e0275a968498dfbe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot\\frac{B}{2}=\\frac{14-x}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"123\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b058d06eaf3b679e9910728628df4a8816a2161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot\\frac{D}{2}=\\frac{12-x}{r}=\\tan\\frac{B}{2}=\\frac{r}{14-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"275\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/324684c936ace1003b2d91db2a323cda6d51fd47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2=\\frac{12-x}{14-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" />. Putting this together with the above equation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/1547baf7548b35cec9409512c4a54d1b2a0bc297.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(12-x)(14-x)=x(x-5)\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/7/ec7dbb203c897ead31adc993f8cec8cd2fec6da9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow x^2-26x+168=x^2-5x\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"16\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/0/da04679d75bdafb05d80887a6c81d17a19b3b8ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow 21x=168\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28d5329133095f2005552a18296c77bd22eb9d42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow x=8.\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645d00d96702d64c17b0618b9eecee2a2f5ae792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2=8(8-5)=8(3)=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"203\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfe79efccfc86efb2d1976a24423fe54cf3148f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\sqrt{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"112\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28wowe.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(wowe)\">Solution 4 (wowe)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (wowe)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the inradius. Then, the area of the quadrilateral can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a017442817811bb8153db9dda0aa9e5c6e1b3009.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Clearly, the larger the area of the quadrilateral, the larger the value of the inradius.\n</p><p><br />\nKnow that the area of a quadrilateral is maximized when it is cyclic. Applying Brahmagupta's, the area will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f15407952a248dcd90889a58c5da978c34181e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(9)(7)(12)(14)} = 42\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"197\" height=\"35\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/7386fbd04078287e343c731b73deb1d0ae6c3e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21r = 42\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8a747d01f6c85693aa6463090c6127e8818c6f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 2\\sqrt6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"114\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>-skibbysiggy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Why are the above solutions so yap buh.\n</p><p>Assume that the quadrilateral is cyclic, because that is how the area fo a quadrilateral with fixed side lengths is maimised.\n</p><p>Recall form googling random geometry theorems for AIME that the area of a bicentric quadrilateral with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dccd892c8fcf49bddefcc3fe1ff23e22115b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{abcd}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"21\" />, and this might seem too good to be true, but it is indeed true, and now we proceed with the solution.\n</p><p>By Pitot's Theorem, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b7a610ca1c6be229c1c4446ebfc737cd3fd1e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB+CD=AD+BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"185\" height=\"14\" />, there exists a circle tangent to all four sides of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, we need to find the radius of this circle. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f6a8dfe6d1a7764e3d737e70a7baa2408be22e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = rs$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> also holds for tangential quadrilaterals, and thus, the area of this tangential quarilateral which is known to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca02ee3e49f09809e9dd078ee51a815dad272bcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dccd892c8fcf49bddefcc3fe1ff23e22115b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{abcd}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"21\" /> formula, has:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72241d2e2cb59332e9b8e65af7f98dfcced8cb05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs = 42\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d1dec8f82aa6b0843f84ad5396c24393eaa7d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\cdot 21 = 42\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b9349b984b324209faaf0c84f0ae999820d58f5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\boxed{2\\sqrt{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"79\" height=\"32\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6dbbac62a58811f44fda1df541fe2d2b7f43bc64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d03964589d6c9d48bbb4ed36acd2e568c899f62a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square{}$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>-cheltstudent\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A\">2011 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017224313\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.057 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 634/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18595/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.803      1 -total\n 59.75%    7.650      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.80%    4.839      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9041:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017224313 and revision id 288552. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}